FILED s531a (Opus 5.5, 2026-11-01) from #1815's probes.  PRE-EXISTING (ade297e7 the same).

REPRO (perl 5.40.3), lib/DiesMod.pm = `package DiesMod; die "dm\n"; 1;`:
  use lib 'lib';
  eval { require DiesMod }; print "err=$@"; print exists $INC{'DiesMod.pm'} ? 1 : 0, defined $INC{'DiesMod.pm'} ? 1 : 0, "\n";
  eval { require DiesMod }; print "again=$@";
perl: err=dm / Compilation failed in require at ...  10  again=Attempt to reload DiesMod.pm aborted. / Compilation failed in require ...
PCL:  err=dm  00  again=dm   -- the module body runs a SECOND time (every side effect twice: a silent wrong for a module that registers, pushes or prints at load).

Two halves: (1) a failed load stores $INC{NAME} = undef (p-use / p-require-file / the hook path; `exists` true, `defined` false); (2) a require that finds an undef entry dies "Attempt to reload NAME aborted.\nCompilation failed in require" (perl's message text is not a goal; the die is).  The "Compilation failed in require" suffix on the FIRST die is text only.  Probe: s531a scratch/s531a/pr/diesmod.pl.  NOTE the #1688 half is separate: a file that returns FALSE leaves %INC ABSENT in perl (probed), which PCL now matches.
